--- Pre-flight: two pre-existing integration breakages on this branch were repaired (NOT caused by SwipeRow) ---
  1. apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been re-concatenated into multiple
     <Project> roots (merge=union, MSB4025) and failed XML load. Regenerated into a single canonical root
     (the case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated union of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs
     on disk under the five surface dirs) + the new SwipeRow Model/Source/ViewModel links. This is the
     documented, predecessor-sanctioned repair (see the file's own INVARIANT comment; 0159/0166/0170/0173/0178).
  2. The committed Breadcrumbs and LayoutBreadcrumbs surfaces both declared BreadcrumbItem /
     IBreadcrumbNavigator / NullBreadcrumbNavigator in namespace TeslaSync.App.SharedSurfaces (CS0101),
     breaking the whole app+test C# compile (which cascaded into 96 XAML WMC0001/WMC9999 errors). Verified
     NO references to these identifiers exist outside the LayoutBreadcrumbs surface + its test, then renamed
     the later surface's three colliding types to LayoutBreadcrumbItem / ILayoutBreadcrumbNavigator /
     NullLayoutBreadcrumbNavigator (fully contained; both surfaces' behaviour + tests preserved).

